<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">United Suvadive Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1959 CE – 1963 CE · capital Hithadhoo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A breakaway state of the southern Maldive atolls that rebelled against Male's control between 1959 and 1963.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Discontent in the three southernmost atolls, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addu-atoll">Addu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huvadhu-atoll">Huvadhu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuvahmulah">Fuvahmulah</a>, over taxes and Male's attempts to restrict trade led to revolt in 1959. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-afeef">Abdullah Afeef</a>, a local leader at Addu, where the British had an air base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gan-addu-atoll">Gan</a>, was declared president of the United Suvadive Republic, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hithadhoo">Hithadhoo</a> as its capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic traded directly with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> and with the British base, and set up its own government and postal system. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> offered tacit support but never granted recognition. The government in Male under prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-nasir">Ibrahim Nasir</a> sent armed forces, which suppressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huvadhu-atoll">Huvadhu</a> rebels in 1962.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The republic was dissolved in 1963, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-afeef">Afeef</a> went into exile in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-seychelles">Seychelles</a> with British help. The atolls returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-the-maldives">Sultanate of the Maldives</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/united-suvadive-republic.jpg" alt="United Suvadive Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Suvadive_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1959 CE – 1963 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hithadhoo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullah Afeef</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dhivehi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/maldives">Maldives</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Suvadive Islands republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1961&amp;focus=united-suvadive-republic" aria-label="United Suvadive Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6710 2200 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where United Suvadive Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7030 2456L7039 2277"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7039 2277h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7030 2456h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7030 2456h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Hithadhoo. <a href="/atlas?year=1961&amp;focus=united-suvadive-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
